{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.RankNullity","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FreeModule.Finite.Matrix","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.octCarrier_finrank_ker_eq_14_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.octCarrier_finrank_ker_eq_14_iff","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DerivationRankNullity.lean#L147-L152","doc":"The `G₂` gate on the concrete carrier: `dim Der = 14 ⟺ rank L = 50`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.octCarrier_finrank_ker_add_finrank_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.octCarrier_finrank_ker_add_finrank_range","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DerivationRankNullity.lean#L139-L145","doc":"`dim Der + rank L = 64` on the concrete carrier, for any candidate\noctonion multiplication `m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.finrank_end_octCarrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.finrank_end_octCarrier","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DerivationRankNullity.lean#L131-L135","doc":"`End(OctCarrier)` is 64-dimensional — the concrete instantiation the\noctonion defect operator lives in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.finrank_octCarrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.finrank_octCarrier","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DerivationRankNullity.lean#L128-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.OctCarrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.OctCarrier","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DerivationRankNullity.lean#L122-L124","doc":"The 8-dimensional coordinate carrier for an octonion algebra over `K`\n(the multiplication is a parameter of the theorems above, not fixed here). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.finrank_ker_eq_14_iff_finrank_range_eq_50","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.finrank_ker_eq_14_iff_finrank_range_eq_50","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DerivationRankNullity.lean#L108-L116","doc":"**The `G₂` dimension gate.** For an 8-dimensional algebra,\n`dim Der = 14 ⟺ rank (leibnizDefect) = 50`: the `dim Der(𝕆) = 14` target is\nequivalent to a rank-50 computation on the 64-dimensional endomorphism\nspace. This is the interface an explicit-basis rank witness plugs into. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.finrank_ker_add_finrank_range_eq_64","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.finrank_ker_add_finrank_range_eq_64","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DerivationRankNullity.lean#L99-L106","doc":"**The octonion-shaped rank–nullity identity**: for any bilinear\nmultiplication on an 8-dimensional space, `dim Der + rank L = 64`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.finrank_end","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.finrank_end","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DerivationRankNullity.lean#L95-L97","doc":"The endomorphism space of an 8-dimensional space is 64-dimensional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.finrank_ker_add_finrank_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.finrank_ker_add_finrank_range","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DerivationRankNullity.lean#L80-L88","doc":"**Rank–nullity for the derivation space** of any finite-dimensional\nalgebra: `dim Der(V, m) + rank (leibnizDefect m) = (dim V)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.mem_ker_leibnizDefect_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.mem_ker_leibnizDefect_iff","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DerivationRankNullity.lean#L72-L78","doc":"Membership in `ker (leibnizDefect m)` is exactly the Leibniz rule: the\nkernel is the derivation space `Der(V, m)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.leibnizDefect_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.leibnizDefect_apply","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DerivationRankNullity.lean#L68-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.leibnizDefect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.DerivationRankNullity.leibnizDefect","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/DerivationRankNullity.lean#L50-L65","doc":"The **Leibniz-defect operator** of a bilinear multiplication `m` on `V`:\n`leibnizDefect m D = (x, y) ↦ D (m x y) − m (D x) y − m x (D y)`, as a linear\nmap from endomorphisms to bilinear maps. Its kernel is the derivation space\n`Der(V, m)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}